   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Long-term in-line advisory support (Deputy Secretary Customs) to Customs and Border Control contributed to a modernised customs regime, and ongoing institutional strengthening of the Nauru Customs Service. The UN-developed customs management and data processing system, the Automated Systems for Customs Data (ASYCUDA), went live in October 2023. This improved the readiness of the Customs Service to implement reform processes. The ASYCUDA database removes the potential for human error by automating fiscal and trade reporting to the government. 
Australia supported Nauru&#x2019;s drafting and review of excise legislation which was passed in Parliament in July 2023. The new legislation enables a shift from import duty as the core revenue for customs. This reform indefinitely secured approximately 74% of customs revenue from any effects of free trade agreements (FTAs) and opens the door for Cabinet to consider future adoption of FTAs such as PACER Plus.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The NRO, under the leadership of an Australia-funded Deputy Secretary Revenue and supported by a Tax Administration Adviser, successfully upgraded and digitised the NRO tax identification number (TIN) registration system in 2023. This upgrade strengthened the integrity and efficiency of the NRO tax system and supported a more robust, secure and accurate taxpayer registration system. It also produced real-time data reports to enable identification of risks to revenue and taxation. Operation of an increasingly efficient revenue management system enabled tax revenue collections to be better accounted for, monitored against budget expectations, and analysed to inform government revenue forecasting.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
